{
 "id": "relation_vocabulary",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "description": "RELATION-VOCABULARY lexicon (graph data) for SIGNATURE-AUTHORING. Each RelationCue node maps DEFINITION-WORDS (keywords found in a held Concept's own grounded definition) to a structural RELATION-TUPLE in the signature relation-vocabulary (build/refers/bound/base/detect/map/invariant/move/reduce/...). The signature-authoring mechanism reads a Concept's OWN definition, finds which cues fire (keyword hit, the same mechanical category as the held ShapePrinciple lexicon / relation perception), and assembles the relation tuples those cues emit into the Concept's structural signature \u2014 which the held bridge matcher (AntiUnify/FixedCount) then compares to faculties. The signature is EARNED from the Concept's own definition text, not hand-written per Concept; this lexicon is the (text -> structural relation) mapping, extensible by adding a RelationCue node.",
